Homepage: https://github.com/tpluharik/tuxdisplay
Description: use an iPad or Android tablet as a GNOME Wayland monitor over USB
 TuxDisplay creates a real extended monitor or mirrors the primary GNOME
 Wayland screen and streams it to OpenDisplay on iPadOS or Android, or to the
 open-source AVNC Android client through an opt-in, password-authenticated,
 device-scoped ADB reverse tunnel. No IP network or Internet connection is
 required. An opt-in browser client binds only loopback and active USB
 interfaces. Other desktop sessions use an
 isolated X11 workspace rather than extending the current desktop.
